1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,500
See 10 sights in a day like China's "special-forces" tourists — or slow right down?
{\fs13}I'm your China Travel Expert

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:07,000
Young travellers invented 特种兵 (tèzhǒngbīng, "special forces") trips: a city in 48 hours.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,300
You take an overnight train, sleep sitting up, and start sightseeing at dawn.

4
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:13,800
Some skip hotels and crash in 24-hour hotpot spots, bathhouses or internet cafes.

5
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:17,200
A local student can guide you on a full-city sprint for about $7 an hour.

6
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:20,400
So which are you — a 48-hour sprint, or one city done slow? Pick your side.
